                <pb facs="0151" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg81"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in Japan,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 27, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Citizens of the United States are informed that in conjunction with my
                    colleagues, I have made arrangements with the Japanese government by which the
                    city of Yedo, the town of Neegata on the west coast, and the harbor of
                    Ebisuminato, on the island of Sado, will be opened to them for trade and
                    residence, pursuant to treaty stipulations, on the first day of April next.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the
                            United States in Japan.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
